Z||000000||8Ball||09-15-2001||04:30 PM||||Yep after 3 weeks I FINALLY got the new water pump finished. Only one problem  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I have to do it all over again. I broke the dang pump by tightening a bolt to tight so I have now removed the new/old one and am getting ready to put the 2nd one on. Should be done in about an hour. I can't believe how fast it is going now. It only took me 30 mins to get it off this time instead of 3 weeks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Anyway Gonna eat and finish up the pump then go for a ride.<BR>Have fun all||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-15-2001||06:52 PM||||What motor are you doing this to/with?<BR>Any tips/tricks that we need to know about?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||8Ball||09-15-2001||06:56 PM||||Was doing it on a 2.8 only advice I have is Don't break the bolts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and do not over tighten the bolts when you put the new one back on. Once it is snug a 1/4 turn more should do it. Oh yea and if you do break a water pump... they will not take it as a core return ||||reg||1
